Make doctrine/common 2.8 quiet on PHP 7.4.

doctrine/common is pinned to 2.8 by doctrine/orm 2.5 (which in turn is pinned
by Symfony 2.8, see patches/doctrine-orm-2.5-php74.patch). Casting a
ReflectionType to string is deprecated as of PHP 7.4, and the proxy generator
does that for every typed parameter and return type it copies into a generated
proxy class. Read the type name through ReflectionNamedType::getName() instead,
which is what doctrine/common 2.10 does.

--- a/lib/Doctrine/Common/Proxy/ProxyGenerator.php
+++ b/lib/Doctrine/Common/Proxy/ProxyGenerator.php
@@ -1040,7 +1040,7 @@
         \ReflectionMethod $method,
         \ReflectionParameter $parameter = null
     ) {
-        $name = (string) $type;
+        $name = $type instanceof \ReflectionNamedType ? $type->getName() : (string) $type;
         $nameLower = strtolower($name);
 
         if ('self' === $nameLower) {
